@startuml registration
title Registration - the core scenario

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor Client
participant "AuthController" as Ctl
participant "RegistrationService" as Svc
participant "PersonServiceGateway" as PGw
participant "person-service" as Per
participant "KeycloakAdminGateway" as AGw
participant "KeycloakOidcGateway" as OGw
participant "Keycloak" as Kc

Client -> Ctl : POST /api/v1/auth/registration
activate Ctl
Ctl -> Svc : register
activate Svc

Svc -> Svc : validate format and\npassword confirmation

Svc -> PGw : create domain user
activate PGw
PGw -> Per : POST /api/v1/persons/registration
Per --> PGw : user_uid
PGw --> Svc : user_uid
deactivate PGw

group Domain user already exists past this line
  Svc -> AGw : create account
  activate AGw
  AGw -> Kc : POST /admin/realms/REALM/users\nno password, plus user_uid attribute
  Kc --> AGw : keycloak user id
  AGw -> Kc : PUT .../users/{id}/reset-password\ntemporary false
  AGw -> Kc : GET .../roles/USER\nPOST .../users/{id}/role-mappings/realm
  AGw --> Svc : keycloak user id
  deactivate AGw

  Svc -> OGw : log in
  activate OGw
  OGw -> Kc : POST /realms/REALM/protocol/openid-connect/token
  Kc --> OGw : access, refresh, expiresIn
  OGw --> Svc : tokens
  deactivate OGw
end

Svc --> Ctl : TokenResponse
deactivate Svc
Ctl --> Client : 201 with tokens and user_uid
deactivate Ctl

note over Svc, Kc
  The order is deliberate: the Keycloak account is
  created only after the domain step succeeded, so
  no account is ever left without a domain user.

  Three admin calls, not one: Keycloak takes the
  password through its own endpoint and hands out no
  role on import. An account left between them is
  removed again - see keycloak-admin-gateway.puml.

  The inverse is the open window. Any failure inside
  the group leaves an orphaned domain user, and the
  compensation policy applies - structured log, mark
  the registration inconsistent, return an error,
  hide nothing.
end note

@enduml
